{"content":"```\nsimplify: 132 SPIR-V instructions, 10 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 0 dead instructions removed\n  15 loads of a variable just stored to became the stored value; 0 stores overwritten before any read removed\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once), beyond what spirv-opt -O and a driver's back end do: 39 -> 30 (-23.1%)\n  counting the strength reductions any driver also does: 88 -> 30 (-65.9%)\n  also done by any driver compiler (6 rewrites, -49; kept in the written module, not counted above): 1 an extract at bit 0 is a mask; 3 a multiply by a power of two is a shift; 1 a divide by a power of two is a shift; 1 a remainder by a power of two is a mask\n  by kind:\n       3  equals its operand                            -7\n       1  always this value                             -2\n  rewrites:\n    %35 = OpExtInst %int %1 SClamp %33 %int_0 %int_255\n      ->  %33   (equals its operand; -4)\n    %42 = OpExtInst %uint %1 UMin %41 %uint_15\n      ->  %41   (equals its operand; -2)\n    %82 = OpULessThan %bool %80 %uint_64\n      ->  true   (always this value; -2)\n    %85 = OpSelect %uint %82 %83 %uint_0\n      ->  %63   (equals its operand; -1)\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\n  the rewritten module is attached as simplified.spvasm\n```","embeds":[],"allowed_mentions":{"parse":[],"roles":[],"users":[],"replied_user":false},"message_reference":{"message_id":"5001","channel_id":"47","guild_id":"7","fail_if_not_exists":false},"attachments":[{"id":"0","filename":"simplified.spvasm","description":"","content_type":"text/plain","size":3774,"url":"","proxy_url":"","ephemeral":false}]}
